WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.320
(suspenseful music)

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:03.570
- Iran-backed groups form a land bridge

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.060
across the Middle East
and connect in an alliance

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:09.030
that Iran calls the Axis of Resistance.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:11.640
Its focus, to oppose the West.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.580
They can both transport
equipment and personnel,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.480
but they can also use these
positions to attack US interests

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.640
or threaten Israel closer to its borders.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.680
The alliance has been brought into focus

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.510
amid the Hamas-Israel War

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.944
as the groups are mobilizing
on multiple fronts.

00:00:26.944 --> 00:00:27.990
- [Cameraperson] Whoa.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.490
- At the same time.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:31.620
So here's how Iran built out the network

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.300
across the Middle East

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.883
and what it means for the US and Israel.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.153
So to show you

00:00:38.153 --> 00:00:41.040
where Iran's so-called
Axis of Resistance works

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.530
in the Middle East, we
have Iran over here,

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:47.110
and then, of course,
Hamas in Gaza over here

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:48.870
on the Mediterranean.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.790
There's another group that Iran supports

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:53.640
in Gaza called the
Palestinian Islamic Jihad,

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.030
which is actually a closer
ally of Iran ideologically,

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.930
but also working out of Gaza
here and also in the West Bank.

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.840
Iran's most important militia ally

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.990
is Hezbollah here in Lebanon.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:07.823
Aside from that,

00:01:07.823 --> 00:01:11.493
they also have Syria's
president, Bashar al-Assad, here,

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.090
and various militant groups in Iraq.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.130
And then, finally, they
also have an alliance

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:21.270
with the Houthis in Yemen down here south.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.920
These connections allow Iran

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.080
to expand its influence in the Middle East

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.460
and make it easier for the country

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.920
to transport military
equipment, personnel,

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.483
and weapons through the region.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.630
One of Iran's aims in the Middle East

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:37.200
is to always keep the
fight or the military fight

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.630
as far away from its
own borders as possible,

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:41.880
and the presence of these military allies

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.610
and the land bridge
kinda helps it do that.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.980
To understand why Iran
has this belt of influence

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.250
in the region, we need
to go back a few decades.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:53.130
Following the Iranian Revolution in 1979,

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.620
Tehran has sought to
exert military, cultural,

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.620
and ideological dominance
across the Middle East.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.080
That led to the creation
of the Quds Force,

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.880
a branch of the Iranian military,

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.223
which was later led by Qassem Soleimani.

00:02:06.164 --> 00:02:07.890
Soleimani became famous in the West

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.090
over the past decade or so,

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:12.720
because Iran decided
to elevate his profile

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.130
as the mastermind,

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.920
the architect behind this modern iteration

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.483
of the Axis of Resistance.

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:23.751
(Qassem speaking foreign language)

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.580
- [Sune] Later, Soleimani was killed

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:35.013
in a drone strike ordered by the US.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:40.560
- Soleimani was plotting
imminent and sinister attacks

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.770
on American diplomats
and military personnel,

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:48.770
but we caught him in the
act and terminated him.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.380
- The strike was aimed at
weakening Iran's ability

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.120
to threaten American interests

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.013
in Iraq and across the region.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.120
But that goal hasn't materialized.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.940
Iran has continued to
supply groups such as Hamas

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.470
with weapons and training.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:05.361
On October 7th,

00:03:05.361 --> 00:03:08.850
Hamas, designated a terror
organization by the US,

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:12.633
launched a broad assault
on Israel, killing 1,200.

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:16.410
Iranian supreme leader, Ali Khamenei,

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.210
said immediately after the attack

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.790
that Iran did not have
a hand in planning it,

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:21.725
but supported it.

00:03:21.725 --> 00:03:24.090
(suspenseful music)

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.010
To try and curb Iran's influence,

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.870
the US works with allied countries

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.000
to have a presence of bases and troops

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.353
across the Middle East.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.400
Of course, Israel here
and Saudi Arabia here

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.190
as its two sort of main and closest allies

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:39.540
against Iranian influence.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:43.740
Jordan has also for very long
been a very firm US ally,

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:47.730
and the US also has partners in the Gulf.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:51.390
The US also has a presence
in some of the countries

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:54.450
where it's competing
for influence with Iran,

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.030
for example, in Iraq, of course,

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:59.640
and the US also still
has a military presence

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.130
in Northern Syria where it's
been allied for many years

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:04.980
with Kurdish forces in the
fight against Islamic state,

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:07.440
but now, also maintains
a military presence

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:10.170
to sort of counter this
Iranian land bridge

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:13.323
or the threat from Iran to
US interests and allies.

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:16.830
Tehran-backed groups
operating in this region

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:20.160
have been particularly
active since October 7th.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.360
So let's remove all of these

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.310
and take a look at what's been happening.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:26.400
On October 7th, Hamas attacked Israel

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:27.780
here on the border with Gaza.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.100
Israel responded with a major
military offensive on Gaza.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.013
But Iran's allies have also responded

00:04:34.013 --> 00:04:37.770
to this Israeli attack
from different sides.

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:39.870
Most importantly, the Hezbollah militia

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.850
in the northern part with Israel

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:46.050
has engaged in skirmishes
with Israeli soldiers.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:49.170
Iranian militias in Syria
have also gotten closer

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:52.200
to the border where they
have engaged in skirmishes.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.350
Down here in Yemen, the
Iranian allied Houthi rebels

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.740
have both fired rockets
at Southern Israel,

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:02.460
but also captured a vessel in the Red Sea.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.860
The Houthis also launched
drones and missiles

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.900
to other commercial vessels in the area.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:10.230
That led to a US-led multinational
task force stepping in

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:11.340
to try and protect one

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.860
of the world's most vital shipping lanes.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.780
And elsewhere, Iranian-backed militias

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:19.260
in Iraq and Syria conducted
nearly 100 rocket attacks

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:22.170
against US forces over the
past two months according

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.190
to the Pentagon.

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:25.920
Even though there's been
these types of attacks

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:29.400
with increased frequency
over the past decade or so,

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:33.540
in this context, of course,
they compound pressure on Israel

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:36.600
and help sort of pressure
Israel in this context

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.128
where they're fighting Hamas and Gaza.

00:05:39.128 --> 00:05:40.470
(suspenseful music)

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:42.210
Although Iran's Axis of Resistance

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.950
has claimed attacks on multiple fronts

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:45.750
amid the Hamas-Israel War,

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.780
Middle East analysts believe
a wider regional conflict

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.313
is unlikely for now.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:52.860
Even though other parts of this alliance

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.890
have distanced themselves
from the October 7th attacks,

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:58.110
the fact that there was
a big attack on Israel

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:00.120
has given the alliance a bit of momentum,

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.610
but also put a little bit
of pressure, to be honest,

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:05.553
on some of the other militant groups,

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:08.610
both to strike a bit of Israel

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:11.220
and to come to the defense
of the Palestinians

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:13.320
who are now on the severe airstrikes

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.303
and the ground invasion in Gaza.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.630
So far, groups in the alliance

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.810
have been sticking to
calculated and strategic strikes

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.510
rather than moves that could
risk a full blown conflict

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.761
with Israel and its allies.

00:06:26.761 --> 00:06:29.761
(suspenseful music)

